              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मात्रा — mātrā — \"a quantity; a measure\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "यदि औषधस्य मात्रा अधिका, तर्हि हानिः भविष्यति। yadi auṣadhasya mātrā adhikā, tarhi hāniḥ bhaviṣyati. If the dose of medicine is too large, it will do harm."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मात्रा (mātrā) comes from the root √mā, \"to measure\"; MW gives mātrā \"measure, quantity, size, duration, degree\" (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
